<title>MEXICO: Mexican daily port, shipping update for July 14.</title>
<headline>Mexican daily port, shipping update for July 14.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>All Mexican ports were open to shipping on Monday, the Communications and Transport Ministry (SCT) said in its 1000 local/1500 GMT daily meteorological report.</p>
<p>Hurricane Enrique was spotted 885 miles (1416 km) off the coast of Baja California, moving west-northwest at 15 knots (16 miles/28 km) with winds from 90 to 110 knots (99 miles/158 km to 121 miles/194 km). Ships were advised against sailing in the region.</p>
<p>Electric storms and strong winds were reported in Oaxaca and Chiapas.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
